{"root_text": {"uid": "kp5", "lang": "en", "is_root": false, "title": "The Greatest Good Fortune", "author": "Bhikkhu Brahmali", "author_short": "Brahmali", "author_uid": "brahmali", "next": {"author_uid": "anandajoti", "lang": "en", "name": "Gems ", "uid": "kp6"}, "previous": {"author_uid": "anandajoti", "lang": "en", "name": "The Boy’s Questions ", "uid": "kp4"}, "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset='UTF-8'>\n<meta name='author' content='Bhikkhu Brahmali'>\n<title></title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<article id='kp5' lang='en'>\n<header>\n<h1 class='sutta'>5. The Greatest Good Fortune</h1>\n</header>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc1' href='#sc1'>SC 1</a><span class='evam'>This is what I have heard</span>. At one time the Blessed One was staying at Sāvatthī in the Jeta Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s Monastery. On that occasion, as the night was coming to an end, a certain god of great beauty approached the Blessed One while illuminating the whole Jeta Grove. After bowing to the Blessed One, they stood to one side and spoke a verse:</p>\n<blockquote class='gatha'>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc2' href='#sc2'>SC 2</a>“Many gods and humans,<br>\nDesiring well-being,<br>\nAre seekers of good fortune:<br>\nPlease tell me the greatest good fortune.”</p>\n</blockquote>\n<blockquote class='gatha'>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc3' href='#sc3'>SC 3</a>“Not to associate with fools,<br>\nBut to associate with the wise,<br>\nAnd to honour those worthy of honour:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc4' href='#sc4'>SC 4</a>“To live in a suitable place,<br>\nHaving previously done good karma,<br>\nAnd to apply oneself in the right way:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc5' href='#sc5'>SC 5</a>“To be educated and to have a vocation,<br>\nTo be well-trained in one’s chosen field,<br>\nAnd to speak words that are well-spoken:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc6' href='#sc6'>SC 6</a>“To support one’s mother and father,<br>\nTo cherish one’s partner and children,<br>\nAnd to have a job without stress:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc7' href='#sc7'>SC 7</a>“Generosity and an upright life,<br>\nKindness towards one’s relatives,<br>\nAnd the doing of blameless deeds:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc8' href='#sc8'>SC 8</a>“To refrain from what is unwholesome,<br>\nTo abstain from all intoxicants,<br>\nAnd to be steadfast in good qualities,<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc9' href='#sc9'>SC 9</a>“Respect and humility,<br>\nContentment and gratitude,<br>\nAnd the timely hearing of Dharma:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc10' href='#sc10'>SC 10</a>“Being patient and easy to correct,<br>\nThe seeing of monks and nuns,<br>\nAnd timely discussion on Dharma:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc11' href='#sc11'>SC 11</a>“Asceticism and the spiritual life,<br>\nInsight into the noble truths,<br>\nAnd the seeing for oneself of Nirvana:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc12' href='#sc12'>SC 12</a>“A mind that remains unshaken<br>\nBy the ups and the downs of the world,<br>\nSorrowless, stainless and safe:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc13' href='#sc13'>SC 13</a>“Having performed these things,<br>\nNowhere can they be conquered—<br>\nThey are secure wherever they go.<br>\nThis is their greatest good fortune.”</p>\n</blockquote>\n<footer>\n<p>Translated by <span class='author'>Bhikkhu Brahmali</span>, <span class='publication-date'>2015</span>.</p>\n<p>Dedicated to the Public Domain by way of Creative Commons Zero (CC0).</p>\n<p>Prepared for SuttaCentral by <span class='editor'>Bhikkhu Sujato</span>.</p>\n</footer>\n</article>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}, "translation": {"uid": "kp5", "lang": "en", "is_root": false, "title": "The Greatest Good Fortune", "author": "Bhikkhu Brahmali", "author_short": "Brahmali", "author_uid": "brahmali", "next": {"author_uid": "anandajoti", "lang": "en", "name": "Gems ", "uid": "kp6"}, "previous": {"author_uid": "anandajoti", "lang": "en", "name": "The Boy’s Questions ", "uid": "kp4"}, "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset='UTF-8'>\n<meta name='author' content='Bhikkhu Brahmali'>\n<title></title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<article id='kp5' lang='en'>\n<header>\n<h1 class='sutta'>5. The Greatest Good Fortune</h1>\n</header>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc1' href='#sc1'>SC 1</a><span class='evam'>This is what I have heard</span>. At one time the Blessed One was staying at Sāvatthī in the Jeta Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s Monastery. On that occasion, as the night was coming to an end, a certain god of great beauty approached the Blessed One while illuminating the whole Jeta Grove. After bowing to the Blessed One, they stood to one side and spoke a verse:</p>\n<blockquote class='gatha'>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc2' href='#sc2'>SC 2</a>“Many gods and humans,<br>\nDesiring well-being,<br>\nAre seekers of good fortune:<br>\nPlease tell me the greatest good fortune.”</p>\n</blockquote>\n<blockquote class='gatha'>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc3' href='#sc3'>SC 3</a>“Not to associate with fools,<br>\nBut to associate with the wise,<br>\nAnd to honour those worthy of honour:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc4' href='#sc4'>SC 4</a>“To live in a suitable place,<br>\nHaving previously done good karma,<br>\nAnd to apply oneself in the right way:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc5' href='#sc5'>SC 5</a>“To be educated and to have a vocation,<br>\nTo be well-trained in one’s chosen field,<br>\nAnd to speak words that are well-spoken:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc6' href='#sc6'>SC 6</a>“To support one’s mother and father,<br>\nTo cherish one’s partner and children,<br>\nAnd to have a job without stress:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc7' href='#sc7'>SC 7</a>“Generosity and an upright life,<br>\nKindness towards one’s relatives,<br>\nAnd the doing of blameless deeds:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc8' href='#sc8'>SC 8</a>“To refrain from what is unwholesome,<br>\nTo abstain from all intoxicants,<br>\nAnd to be steadfast in good qualities,<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc9' href='#sc9'>SC 9</a>“Respect and humility,<br>\nContentment and gratitude,<br>\nAnd the timely hearing of Dharma:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc10' href='#sc10'>SC 10</a>“Being patient and easy to correct,<br>\nThe seeing of monks and nuns,<br>\nAnd timely discussion on Dharma:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc11' href='#sc11'>SC 11</a>“Asceticism and the spiritual life,<br>\nInsight into the noble truths,<br>\nAnd the seeing for oneself of Nirvana:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc12' href='#sc12'>SC 12</a>“A mind that remains unshaken<br>\nBy the ups and the downs of the world,<br>\nSorrowless, stainless and safe:<br>\nThis is the greatest good fortune.</p>\n<p><a class='ref sc' id='sc13' href='#sc13'>SC 13</a>“Having performed these things,<br>\nNowhere can they be conquered—<br>\nThey are secure wherever they go.<br>\nThis is their greatest good fortune.”</p>\n</blockquote>\n<footer>\n<p>Translated by <span class='author'>Bhikkhu Brahmali</span>, <span class='publication-date'>2015</span>.</p>\n<p>Dedicated to the Public Domain by way of Creative Commons Zero (CC0).</p>\n<p>Prepared for SuttaCentral by <span class='editor'>Bhikkhu Sujato</span>.</p>\n</footer>\n</article>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}, "segmented": false, "suttaplex": {"acronym": "Kp 5", "alt_acronym": null, "volpages": "